  "major": "musical-theatre-bfa-nyc-40864705",
  "major_name": "Musical Theatre",
  "degree": "BFA",
  "campus": "New York",
  "college": "College of Arts, Media and Design",
  "overview_text": "The Bachelor of Fine Arts in Musical Theatre is designed to cultivate the next generation of versatile and innovative performers. This program combines an immersive education with a globally focused liberal arts education that provides students with the artistic and technical skills required to pursue a career in the performing arts. Through rigorous training and practical experience, students have an opportunity to develop the skills necessary to excel in various facets of the industry, primarily acting, singing, and dancing. This program is intended for aspiring performers who are passionate about musical theatre and seek to refine their craft in a structured and supportive environment. Ideal candidates are those with a strong dedication to developing their artistic abilities and who are eager to engage in both creative exploration and professional development. Students may come from diverse backgrounds but share a common goal of pursuing a career in musical theatre.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences Requirements\nAll undergraduate students enrolled in programs at the New York campus are required to fulfill\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences requirements\n.\nMajor Required Courses\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nTHTR 1111\nStagecraft\n4\nTHTR 2020\nVoice and Speech for the Actor 1\n4\nTHTR 2040\nVoice and Speech for the Actor 2\n4\nTHTR 2110\nActing: Process and Technique\n4\nTHTR 2120\nBeginning Scene Study\n4\nTHTR 2150\nScript Analysis\n4\nTHTR 2280\nMusical Theatre Techniques 1\n4\nTHTR 2290\nMusical Theatre Techniques 2\n4\nTHTR 2450\nTheatre Histories 1: Early Evidence Through 1750\n4\nTHTR 2455\nTheatre Histories 2: 1750 Through Tomorrow\n4\nTHTR 2740\nFundamentals of Musical Theatre 1\n4\nTHTR 2745\nFundamentals of Musical Theatre 2\n4\nTHTR 3110\nShakespeare, the Stage, and Humanity\n4\nTHTR 3305\nScene into Song 1\n4\nTHTR 3310\nScene into Song 2\n4\nTHTR 3550\nDirecting for the Stage\n4\nTHTR 4240\nThe Musical Theatre Song Portfolio\n4\nTHTR 4280\nProfessional Preparation: Musical Theatre\n4\nTHTR 4410\nActing: Intermediate Scene Study\n4\nTHTR 4420\nActing: Advanced Scene Study\n4\nTHTR 4650\nAdvanced Studies in Drama and Theatre\n4\nGeneral Electives/NUpath\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete any remaining semester hours after major to fulfill NUpath courses and to reach the minimum semester-hour program requirement.\nMusical Theatre Major Credit Requirement\nComplete 84 semester hours in the major.\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required",
